You have the dry form of age-related macular degeneration. This condition affects the macula, the central part of the retina that provides detailed straight-ahead vision for reading, recognizing faces, and fine tasks.\
\
The most common form is the dry form, which usually progresses slowly. It may not affect your vision in early stages. A smaller number of people develop the wet form, in which abnormal leaking blood vessels grow under the macula, which can cause serious vision loss.\
\
